            <ArticleTitle>Successful treatment of a ruptured spontaneous dissecting coronary artery pseudoaneurysm with a covered stent in a patient with cardiac tamponade.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1067-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The rupture of spontaneous dissecting coronary artery pseudoaneurysms is rare, and no standard therapy has yet been established for this condition. This report describes a case of a ruptured spontaneous dissecting coronary artery pseudoaneurysm in a patient with cardiac tamponade that was successfully treated with emergent implantation of a covered stent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
